"Centrifugal Compressor Design and Similarity Analysis

A centrifugal turbocompressor designed for best performance at the following nominal conditions:
  - Working fluid: dry clean air
  - Inlet pressure and temperature: 1 bar and 20 C
  - Discharge pressure: 2.5 bar
  - Flow rate: 6000 m3/h
  - Flow coefficient: phi = 0.3
  - Head coefficient: psi = 1.4

Determine:
  - The optimal impeller diameter and rotation speed;
  - The diameter and rotation speed for a similar compressor compressing
    12000 m3/h of methane from 2 bar, 20 C to 3 bar.

SOLVER NOTE: Newton solver fails (Singular Jacobian on blk1). Use the full
solver pipeline (TrustRegion or subsequent solvers work correctly).
The default solver configuration includes TrustRegion and will converge.
"
"!Determination of optimal rotation speed N and impeller diameter"
p_su=1E5
t_su=20
p_ex=2.5E5
V_dot_su=6000/3600
phi=0.3
psi=1.4
phi=V_dot_su/(U*A)
U=pi*D*N
A=pi*D^2/4
rpm=N*60
psi=DELTAh_s/(U^2/2)
DELTAh_s=h_exs-h_su
h_su=ENTHALPY(Air,T=T_su)
h_exs=ENTHALPY(Air,s=s_su,p=p_ex)
s_su=ENTROPY(Air,T=T_su,P=P_su)

"Solution:
Variables in Main
A=0.01566 
D=0.1412 
DELTAh_s=88103 
h_exs=381638 [J/kg]
h_su=293534 [J/kg]
N=799.7 
phi=0.3 
psi=1.4 
p_ex=250000 
p_su=100000 
rpm=47985 
s_su=5682 [J/kg-K]
t_su=20 
U=354.8 
V_dot_su=1.667 
"

